  "challenge": {
    "title": "Bargaining and Getting There",
    "instructions": "Write and say a short Damascene conversation that lasts at least 10 lines. It must include asking the price of something, bargaining it down at least once, agreeing on a price, hailing a taxi or asking about a bus, saying where you want to go, and asking about the fare or the time. Use at least 8 target phrases from Unit 3 and include both a masculine-address form and a feminine-address form.",
    "required_elements": [
      "A price question using قديش هاد؟ or بكم الكيلو؟",
      "At least one attempt to lower the price, using خفف شوي or في خصم؟",
      "An agreement using ماشي or آخر سعر.",
      "Hailing transport using فاضي؟ or naming تكسي or باص.",
      "A destination using بدي روح عـ... or خدني عـ...",
      "A question about fare or time using قديش الأجرة؟ or قديش بياخد الطريق؟",
      "Both a masculine-address form (such as عندك) and a feminine-address form (such as عندكِ or تفضلي)."
